    "body": "### Problem\n\nWhen a config's `root_dir` is a function, `vim.lsp.enable()` starts the client in a `vim.schedule` callback once `root_dir` calls back. If the buffer is wiped before that runs, it errors:\n\n```\nvim.schedule callback: vim/fs:483: Invalid buffer id: 2\nstack traceback:\n\t[C]: in function '__index'\n\tvim/fs:483: in function 'root'\n\t.../Cellar/neovim/0.12.6/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/lsp.lua:749: in function 'start_config'\n\t.../Cellar/neovim/0.12.6/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/lsp.lua:564: in function <.../Cellar/neovim/0.12.6/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/lsp.lua:563>\n```\n\n### Steps to reproduce using \"nvim --clean -u minimal_init.lua\"\n\n```lua\nvim.lsp.config('repro', {\n  cmd = { 'cat' },\n  filetypes = { 'repro' },\n  root_markers = { '.git' },\n  root_dir = function(_, on_dir)\n    on_dir()\n  end,\n})\nvim.lsp.enable('repro')\n\nlocal buf = vim.api.nvim_create_buf(true, false)\nvim.bo[buf].filetype = 'repro'\nvim.api.nvim_buf_delete(buf, { force = true })\n```\n\n1. `nvim --clean -u minimal_init.lua`\n2. The error shows on startup\n\n`cmd` only needs to be executable, since the client never starts.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nNo error, and no client started for the wiped buffer.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nv0.12.6, and `lsp_enable_callback` is the same on master\n\n### Language server name/version\n\nNone needed, the error comes before the server starts\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nUbuntu 24.04 (WSL2)\n",
